 "text": "Hi, how you doing? Get the tent down and find a spot against the side of the hill, protected by the hill itself. That's good. Don' stand directly under the tent, look after it has hold all the sides down with cords. Be careful, thunder can make them burst into flame. Yes, pack it up while there's enough light left. Then carry it up the hill a little, for the still stronger wind up there. Look for big rocks and sit on them, or find a tree. Stay as far from the tent as you can. Check the tent in the morning, and let me know if you need help.",
